The second posting was :


>Th second problem now is to introduce the enabler code even after issuing 
>the DECNSR-NET-SVR pak, it seems that NSR considers that there is always a 
>base license.

Once more the French CSC has resolved the problem. 
When you receive your first enabler codes (after having sent your lmf 
listing to Networker_LMFdatabase@zso.dec.com) there are 2 enabler 
certificates with some explanations. It doesn't work if you follow the 
explanations.

1) shutdown NSR
2) remove the DECNSR-NET-SVR pak 
3) issue the following commands

/usr/opt/networker/bin/nsrcap -v -u enabler_code_for_nsr_server
/usr/opt/networker/bin/nsrcap -v -c enabler_code_for_nsr_snmp

Now you are able to see the correct information with nwadmin Menu Server , 
choice registration and it's possible to send the correct information to 
networker@mail.dec.com.

Daniel


