[Original Question]
> 
> I'm trying to install 4.0D on an AlphaStation 500au.
> 
> I updated the firmware to v6.6-29 using Firmware Update V5.0, booted
> from the CD and ran the setup (repartitioned the disk).
> 
> However the base software can't be installed, with this error repeating:
> 
> CAMLogger: cam_error packet
> :bus2
> isp_intr
> write Data Overrun detected - reset SCSI bus to recover
> cam_logger: bus2 target 0 lun 0
> ss_perform_timeout
> timeout on disconnected request
> 
> There is only one disk listed:
> 
> >>>show device
> dka0.0.04.0 	dka0 toshiba CD-ROM
> ...
> ewa0.0.0.3.0	 EWA0 	<mac address>
> 
> ...

--------------------------------------------------------------------------

Thanks to:

  "Alan Rollow - Dr. File System's Home for Wayward Inodes."
     <alan@nabeth.cxo.dec.com>
and
 
  "Dr. Tom Blinn, 603-884-0646" <tpb@doctor.zk3.dec.com>

who pointed me to the right direction.


I found what went wrong myself:

I setup ewa0 (ethernet port) as the boot device, and there happened to be
a major network disruption during the installation, hence the timeout.

I've changed to DKC0 (dkc0.0.0.1009.0 DKC0 RZ1CC-BA 883F) and everything
is fine now.

Thanks again.


Jie

