> It's implemented as part of the timezone setup.  If you change the timezone
> setting to one that doesn't do summer time, then the system won't display the
> local time with summer time adjustment.  If summer time is normally applied in
> your local geography (that is, the "official" time zone), then you might need
> to create your own time zone definition file for your local needs.  Take a
> look at the script in /sbin/it.d/bin that gets the initial time zone value
> during system setup; it will point you in the right direction.
