From tru64-unix-managers  Tue Oct 13 17:36:30 1998
From: Jean-Loup Risler <risler () genetique ! uvsq ! fr>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 1998 17:36:30 +0000
To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: [SUMMARY] NCD keyboard again
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96078724211816

Dear all,

My original message:

----------------
Some time ago, I had problems with my NCD X-tube: the DEL key (well,
the large key at the upper right corner of the main keyboard) erased
the *next* character within Netscape (and Netscape mail).

This was fixed thanks to John Deacon who suggested to add the following
lines in .Xdefaults:

blah blah

Now, I have just installed WORDPERFECT on my 2100 server running
DU 4.0B ... and the very same problem appears again within Wordperfect.
I have also tried the solution suggested by John Clarke which is to set
the "Setup/Change user preferences/Compatibility" to "Be Compatible with
Old DECwindows Vendor String" in the NCD user service console, but to no
avail.
--------------------

I received a suggestion from Terry Horsnell:

xmodmap -e "keycode 0x66 =  Delete BackSpace"

which did not work ... but this made me think that I should "man
xmodmap" and "man xev".

Finally, the solution was to add the following line in .login:

xmodmap -e "keycode 102 = BackSpace Delete"

For the moment, everything seems fine....

Cheers,

Jean-Loup


