Dear Gurus,

Some time ago, I had problems with my NCD X-tube: the DEL key (well,
the large key at the upper right corner of the main keyboard) erased
the *next* character within Netscape (and Netscape mail).

This was fixed thanks to John Deacon who suggested to add the following
lines in .Xdefaults:

*XmText.translations: #override \n\
     Shift<Key>osfDelete:      delete-next-character()\n\
     <Key>osfDelete:           delete-previous-character()\n

*XmTextField.translations:    #override \n\
     Shift<Key>osfDelete:      delete-next-character()\n\
     <Key>osfDelete:           delete-previous-character()\n


Now, I have just installed WORDPERFECT on my 2100 server running
DU 4.0B ... and the very same problem appears again within Wordperfect.
I have also tried the solution suggested by John Clarke which is to set
the "Setup/Change user preferences/Compatibility" to "Be Compatible with
Old DECwindows Vendor String" in the NCD user service console, but to no
avail.

How can I fix this irritating "feature" ?

Thanks and cheers,

Jean-Loup

