My original message is:

"Hello all!

> I have a dual redundant pair of HSZ50s and I am considering buying another
> pair for the new drives that I'm going to purchase. The firmware that I
> have
> on my current pair is 5.1 with patches 1 through 4 on them. I'm not
> certain
> if I want to buy the firmware update service on all four of my HSZ50s
> since
> the upgrades for it don't come out very often. What I need to know is
> which
> version of the HSZ50 firmware is year 2000 compliant so that I can at
> least
> get that running. I'm also open to any advice on if I should get the
> firmware update service or not.
> 
> Thanks!"
> 
> 
I received few responses on this one, so I went ahead and placed a call to
StorageWorx support who said that the Y2K version of the HSZ50 firmware is
versions 5.1 and above. According to Stephen Mullin, the most current
version of the firmware is 5.3, but the StorageWorx people told me that it's
5.2. The StorageWorx folks also said that the major difference between 5.1
and 5.2 is that 5.2 allows you to use the Ultra SCSI 9.1 and 18.2 gig disk
drives. 

Thanks to those who responded!

-Stephen Spalding

