Here some hints (not all tested):

0) installed Mediachanger-Software CLC31x ?
1) Licensing issues (jukeboxes need license -  JUKEBOX-TIER-1 in your
case)
2) You may need to delete the old jukebox from the nsr configuration(via
nwadmin or whatever).
3) jb_config program
4) Does 'file /dev/mcxy' return a proper string ?
The jukebox at our site responds with (after 'file /dev/mcxy'): 
character special (53/17472) SCSI #1 TZ Media special_device #rr (SCSI
ID#a) (SCSI LUN #b). If you get only 'character special' you should
verify that the device created for the jukebox is the correct one.
5) find out the major and minor number of your device :
# file nrmt2h you'll get output something like this :
nrmt0h: character special (9/37891) SCSI #2 TZ887 tape #3 (SCSI ID #5) 
(SCSI LUN #0) loader 62500_bpi
take note of the number in bracket.
then remove the device file:
# rm nrmt2h
and build it again :
# makenod nrmt2h c 9 37891 
(replace these number with what you get from your output)

